From fbccdbd0e84054e3b598452ef1153efb3c4ca26d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:16:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a park awaiting a card re-probes when that
 card's status changes on the same gateway

Incident (2026-11-13, t_01a1d5def756990d): PR #2351's owner t_01a1d4bde1a32381 parked on worker-5 at
16:34:42 with wake_check `hermes kanban wait-check task t_01a1d5c2abb6dcee` (awaiting kind=card,
check_every 900). The review card was created, claimed and completed on worker-5 itself at 16:43:01; the
owner got condition_met only on its regular probe at 16:50:05 (7 min 04 s idle).

Five whys: the owner slept because its probe was not due -> nothing moved next_at earlier -> PR #2370's
expedite has one call site, the sync client's replica pull -> a status change written on this gateway's own
board never goes through a replica pull -> status writes are spread over ~40 `UPDATE tasks SET status`
sites with no single transition helper, so nothing hooked them.

Fix: every outer kanban `write_txn` arms a per-connection TEMP trigger (as kanban_sync_own_writes does)
that records `UPDATE OF status ON tasks` changes in a temp table; they commit and roll back with the write.
After COMMIT, `kanban_local_status_wake.flush` hands this commit's {card: new status} to the same
`kanban_awaited_card_wake.expedite`: next_at earlier only, park re-checked as scheduled inside expedite's
write txn, wake_dispatcher(). One indexed prefilter query (does any scheduled park's probe or park event
mention a changed card?) runs first, so a commit no park cares about never reads every park. Best-effort:
any failure is logged and the transition stands; the park keeps its check_every cadence. No polling.

Proof (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_local_status_wake.py, 18 tests):
- a. complete / block / request_review / archive of the awaited card on this gateway, with the plain
  `wait-check task X` park and with awaiting kind=card ref X: next_at <= t0+60 and the owner is ready on the
  next tick; a file-probe park with only an awaiting card ref also moves.
- b. 30 simulated minutes with other cards changing status and the awaited card getting title edits: 3
  probes (t0, +900, +1800), the same as main.
- c. `--from blocked|review|triage`: an unmet intermediate change costs one probe, then check_every again.
- guards: rolled-back transition, a commit no park mentions (expedite never called), a raising expedite,
  the prefilter cap, a db without tasks.
RED on origin/main 9bd665a43a: 14 failed / 4 passed (b and the no-op guards pass on main, as intended).
GREEN: 18 passed, plus test_kanban_awaited_card_wake.py 14 passed.
